The study focuses on the behavior of solutions, particularly in the area of $(0,\infty)^2$ where singularities may arise. The work provides an explicit solution formula and reveals the conditions under which blow-up occurs along specific curves. The implications of this finding are discussed in the context of related models used to study population dynamics.

